 34S  c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2005Ma03:                          
 34S  c  Phys Rev C 71, 014316 (2005)                                           
 34S  c  Compiled by J. Roediger and B. Singh (McMaster), February 28, 2005     
 34S  c  E=70 MeV.  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, |g|g(|q), |g(|q), lifetimes with   
 34S 2c  |g-spectrometer GASP, which consisted of an array of 40                
 34S 3c  Compton-suppressed HPGe detectors and a multiplicity filter or 80 BGO  
 34S 4c  scintillators.  For the purposes of channel selection and kinematical  
 34S 5c  reconstruction, the 4|p charged-particle detector ISIS (consisting of  
 34S 6c  40 |DE-E Si telescopes) was also used.  DSAM analysis for lifetimes    
 34S  cG $R(ado)=I{-|g1}(at 34|' gated by |g{-2})/I{-|g1}(at 90|' gated by      
 34S 2cG |g{-2}); the gate on the |g{-2} transition is set on the axis where all
 34S 3cG the detectors are added together. Ado ratios were obtained for |g-rays 
 34S 4cG whose low statistics did not allow for the determination of full       
 34S 5cG angular distributions.                                                 
 34S  cG M$For stretched |DJ=1, dipole and |DJ=2 transitions, Q transitions,    
 34S 2cG R(ado)|?0.75 and |?1.25, respectively.                                 
 34S  cG M(X)$A pure M1 character was assumed for this |DJ=1 transition, as the 
 34S 2cG corresponding R(ado) values indicate negligible small mixing.          
 34S  cL E$From least-squares fit to E|g's (by compilers)                       
